      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\nMethodNode draws the effect summary and uses scriptRunnerResult. methodEffects normalizes declarations and usePluginRuntime calls enforceDeclaredEffects. The current HOST_CALL_EFFECTS mapping gates updateNode and updateView; other calls retain existing host checks. Method cards are edit-mode only.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nEffect declarations currently describe more operations than the targeted enforcement mapping covers. This is an implementation gap, not a full sandbox guarantee. Extending enforcement needs a separate runtime task and negative tests per operation.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/Nodes/MethodNode.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/methodEffects.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/hooks/usePluginRuntime.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/methodEffects.test.js`\n- `tests/methodEffectsHost.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-method",
          "nodeId": "method-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
